From eacf0d4f49590727d356161bb22edb3f79eb1fc1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WinTone <mertbay295@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 05:58:45 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] platform/x86: hp-wmi: Add OMEN 16-ap0xxx (8D24) board

The OMEN 16-ap0xxx family already has two entries in the board list,
added by commit 0aab31d47c2e ("platform/x86: hp-wmi: Add support for
Omen 16-ap0xxx (8D26)") and commit 56b7981c6f21 ("platform/x86: hp-wmi:
Add support for Omen 16-ap0xxx (8E35)"). HP ships a third revision under
the same family, board 8D24, which is not listed, so it gets neither the
platform profile nor the hwmon PWM control.

The protocol was recovered from this machine's DSDT and matches what the
driver already implements for its siblings:

  - WMI command group 0x20008 with the "SECU" signature
  - 0x2D fan speed read, 0x2E fan speed write (EC 0x34/0x35)
  - 0x26/0x27 max fan (EC 0xEC bit 2)
  - 0x1A power profile, writing EC 0x95

omen_v1_legacy_board_params is the right parameter set, and not only by
family: its ec_tp_offset is HP_OMEN_EC_THERMAL_PROFILE_OFFSET (0x95),
which is where this board's DSDT places the HPCM field. The alternatives
do not fit - omen_v1 uses 0x59, which on this board is a temperature
register. The profile byte values were captured from the vendor software
on Windows (0x30 balanced, 0x31 performance) and match the driver's
omen_v1 enum.

Tested on an OMEN Gaming Laptop 16-ap0xxx, BIOS F.11, kernel 7.2.4.
Before the patch there is no pwm1 and hp-wmi registers no platform
profile handler. After it, pwm1 appears, the handler registers alongside
amd-pmf, and EC 0x95 reads back 48 (0x30) with the profile set to
balanced - the same value the vendor software writes on Windows.

Signed-off-by: WinTone <mertbay295@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c b/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
index b2773fc..f1ef61c 100644
--- a/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
+++ b/drivers/platform/x86/hp/hp-wmi.c
@@ -319,6 +319,10 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id hp_wmi_feature_boards[] __initconst = {
 		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8C9C") },
 		.driver_data = (void *)&victus_s_board_params,
 	},
+	{
+		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8D24") },
+		.driver_data = (void *)&omen_v1_legacy_board_params,
+	},
 	{
 		.matches = { DMI_MATCH(DMI_BOARD_NAME, "8D26") },
 		.driver_data = (void *)&omen_v1_legacy_board_params,
-- 
2.55.0

